AHS-013 — Cognitive Processing Model

Document ID: AHS-013
Title: Cognitive Processing Model
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Process, Logical, Information

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical cognitive processing model of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Cognitive Processing Model describes how Atlas transforms engineering artifacts through successive cognitive operations while preserving semantic integrity, engineering context, traceability, explainability, and confidence.

It establishes the normative processing behavior implemented by all Atlas cognitive engines.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Cognitive processing stages
Processing operations
Input/output contracts
Processing invariants
Processing lifecycle
Processing quality requirements

This specification is independent of implementation technologies and algorithms.

3. Canonical Definition

Cognitive Processing is the systematic transformation of engineering artifacts into higher-value engineering cognition through a sequence of governed processing operations that preserve semantic integrity and engineering traceability.

4. Processing Objectives

Atlas cognitive processing SHALL:

Transform engineering information into engineering cognition.
Preserve engineering semantics.
Maintain end-to-end traceability.
Maintain explainability.
Maintain engineering context.
Produce deterministic engineering artifacts where applicable.
Support iterative refinement.
