6. Processing Operations
6.1 Acquire
Purpose

Receive engineering artifacts from internal or external sources.

Inputs
Engineering Reality
External systems
Human input
Previous cognitive stages
Outputs

Canonical Engineering Artifacts.

6.2 Validate
Purpose

Verify completeness, correctness, and consistency.

Validation includes:

Structural validation
Semantic validation
Constraint validation
Context validation
Evidence validation

Invalid artifacts SHALL NOT continue.

6.3 Interpret
Purpose

Determine engineering meaning.

Interpretation transforms validated engineering information into Engineering Understanding consistent with ACC-007.

6.4 Integrate
Purpose

Combine new understanding with existing Engineering Memory and Engineering Knowledge.

Integration SHALL:

Detect conflicts.
Preserve provenance.
Merge compatible cognition.
Identify unresolved inconsistencies.
6.5 Reason
Purpose

Apply Engineering Reasoning (ACC-010) to derive justified Engineering Conclusions.

Reasoning SHALL reference:

Engineering Understanding
Engineering Knowledge
Engineering Context
Engineering Constraints
6.6 Evaluate
Purpose

Assess the quality of generated conclusions.

Evaluation SHALL consider:

Confidence
Constraint compliance
Completeness
Consistency
Explainability
Traceability

Outputs failing evaluation SHALL be refined or rejected.

6.7 Apply
Purpose

Execute Engineering Capabilities (ACC-011) using validated conclusions.

Application MAY include:

Analysis
Optimization
Prediction
Planning
Recommendation generation
6.8 Communicate
Purpose

Generate Decision Support (ACC-012).

Communication SHALL provide:

Recommendations
Supporting evidence
Engineering rationale
Confidence
Alternatives
Assumptions
Constraints
7. Processing Invariants

Throughout every processing operation the following SHALL remain preserved:

Artifact identity
Engineering context
Engineering intent
Engineering constraints
Confidence
Traceability
Explainability
Version history

Processing SHALL NOT remove these attributes.

8. Processing Modes

Atlas supports multiple processing modes.

Sequential

Operations execute in order.

Incremental

New information updates existing cognition.

Batch

Multiple artifacts processed collectively.

Streaming

Continuous processing of engineering events.

Interactive

Human-guided processing.

Collaborative

Multiple cognitive engines contribute to a shared outcome.

