10. Processing Outcomes

Processing MAY produce:

Engineering Understanding
Engineering Memory
Engineering Knowledge
Engineering Conclusions
Engineering Recommendations
Decision Support Artifacts

Every outcome SHALL preserve provenance.

11. Failure Handling

Processing failures SHALL:

Preserve intermediate artifacts.
Record failure details.
Maintain traceability.
Support controlled recovery.
Prevent invalid cognition from propagating.
12. Conformance

An implementation conforms if it:

Implements the canonical processing operations.
Preserves processing invariants.
Maintains artifact integrity.
Applies required quality gates.
Produces traceable engineering outcomes.
13. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Domain-specific processing operations.
AI-assisted processing techniques.
Distributed processing models.
Autonomous optimization.
Specialized engineering cognition pipelines.

Extensions SHALL preserve the canonical processing semantics.